# React SuperAdmin Project Rules

## General Guidelines

### NO EMOJIS
- **Never use emojis** in code, comments, documentation, or commit messages
- Simply remove emojis entirely - no replacements like [OK], [FAIL], etc.
- Only allow `x` or `✓` in tables for checkmarks
- All other emojis must be removed from all files

### Code Style
- Use TypeScript with strict mode
- Prefer ES modules over CommonJS
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Add JSDoc comments for public APIs
- Keep functions small and focused

### Documentation
- Write clear, concise documentation
- Use proper Markdown/MDX formatting
- Include code examples for all components
- Keep documentation up-to-date with code changes

### Git Practices
- Use conventional commit messages
- Keep commits focused and atomic
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Use feature branches for new development

### Testing
- Aim for 90%+ test coverage
- Write tests for all public APIs
- Use descriptive test names
- Test both success and error cases

### Performance
- Optimize bundle size
- Use lazy loading where appropriate
- Minimize re-renders
- Profile and optimize critical paths

## Project-Specific Rules

### React SuperAdmin Framework
- Components should be reusable and composable
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all props
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Follow accessibility best practices
- Use semantic HTML elements

### Documentation System
- Keep "Last Built" dates accurate and meaningful
- Use Git commit dates for file modification tracking
- Maintain consistent formatting across all docs
- Include live examples where possible
- Last Built script must run in CI before docs deployment

### Build System
- Ensure all builds pass CI checks
- Keep dependencies up-to-date
- Use pnpm for package management
- Maintain clean build outputs
